12. Semantic Hyperlink vs Jargon

Jargon compresses terminology.

Semantic Hyperlinks should compress executable relational structure.

Bad:

HAMMER = fancy word meaning "analyze"

Good:

HAMMER = reconstructable transformation
         with invariants
         bounds
         expected behavior
         and testable consequences

A valid Semantic Hyperlink should change what the receiver DOES, not merely the vocabulary it uses.

