13. Test Protocol

A link is not validated because it sounds meaningful.

Test it.

Test A — Compression

Compare:

full specification

against:

semantic hyperlink

Measure token reduction.

⸻

Test B — Reconstruction

Give the compressed link to a receiver with the required semantic seed.

Check whether the intended operation is reconstructed.

⸻

Test C — Vocabulary Removal

Remove Pantheon terminology from the resulting output.

If capability disappears with the terminology, the link may only be producing style imitation.

⸻

Test D — Transfer

Test on an unrelated domain.

A strong operator link should preserve its relational function across multiple contexts.

⸻

Test E — Drift

After repeated usage, reconstruct the full checksum.

Compare it to the canonical invariants.

current reconstruction
vs
canonical mechanism

If divergence is excessive:

RESYNCHRONIZE

